{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  "entry": [
    "src/app/**/{page,layout,not-found,error,loading,template,default}.tsx",
    "scripts/*.{ts,mjs}",
    "e2e/**/*.spec.ts",
    "**/*.test.ts",

    /*
      tokens.ts is a real entry point, not an exception.

      `generate-tokens.mjs` consumes roughly fifteen of its exports through a
      `tsx -e` string, which no static analyser can follow. Declaring it as an
      entry states what is true; adding its exports to an ignore list would have
      stated something false and hidden the same fact.
    */
    "src/lib/design/tokens.ts!"
  ],

  "project": ["src/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "scripts/**/*.{ts,mjs}", "e2e/**/*.ts"],

  /*
    DECLARED BLIND SPOT — src/db is not covered by unused-export analysis.

    `db/schema/index.ts` is an `export *` barrel and `db/index.ts` consumes it
    as `import * as schema`, because that namespace is exactly what Drizzle needs
    to build its query API. A namespace import marks every export in the tree as
    used by construction, so knip cannot distinguish a live table from a dead one
    here and reports the whole tree clean either way.

    Verified with a planted export: it is not flagged with the Drizzle plugin on
    or off, so this is a property of the barrel, not of the plugin.

    Deliberately NOT added to `ignore` below — knip correctly points out that
    would be a no-op, since nothing there is ever reported anyway. Writing a
    redundant ignore to look thorough would be config that lies. The gap is
    recorded here and in ADR 0006 instead, because "the run was quiet" is not
    evidence that coverage is intact.
  */

  "ignore": [
    // Vendored shadcn primitives. Retokenized as each is touched; not ours to prune.
    "src/components/ui/**"
  ],

  "ignoreDependencies": [
    "tw-animate-css",
    "tailwindcss",
    "eslint-config-next",
    // Consumed only by the vendored primitives under src/components/ui, ignored above.
    "class-variance-authority",
    "shadcn"
  ],

  /*
    Exports written ahead of their consumer carry `@reserved phase-N`.

    The tag must name a phase, and `scripts/check-phase-references.mjs` fails if
    that phase is not in the PHASES union. Same discipline as the orphaned-term
    register and the bundle budget: an exception is declared, dated, and
    greppable, or it is not an exception.
  */
  "tags": ["-@reserved"],

  /*
    The Drizzle plugin loads drizzle.config.ts, which throws without a
    DATABASE_URL. It printed two ERROR lines on every green run, and a gate that
    cries wolf gets switched off. Disabling it costs nothing: src/db is a
    declared blind spot above for an unrelated and more fundamental reason.
  */
  "drizzle": false,

  "rules": {
    "files": "error",
    "exports": "error",
    "types": "error",
    "duplicates": "error",
    "dependencies": "error",
    "unlisted": "error",
    "binaries": "warn",
    "enumMembers": "off"
  }
}
